/*  How this project's own Cufet tools are built.  Run it with:  cufet build

    ★★ Running this file builds NOTHING. It defines `blueprint` and calls nothing, so what comes
    out is a plan; `cufet build` is what walks it. `cufet blueprint.cufe` gives no output and no
    compilation, which is correct rather than a bug.

    ★ It describes what CUFET builds, not what builds Cufet. The .NET solution produces the `cufet`
    this file needs, so it cannot be a step here — that stays `dotnet build`, see CONTRIBUTING.

    ⚠ The steps run `cufet` from PATH, so this needs one at least as new as the checkout.
    CONTRIBUTING says what an older one looks like when it fails, and how to build without PATH.

    ★★ Nothing below declares that anything depends on anything. `needs` and `makes` are all there
    is, and both tools name `tools/terminal.cufe` — so editing it rebuilds both, and nothing had to
    say so. Staleness is by content: a step is skipped when everything it needs hashes to what it
    hashed last time and everything it makes is still there. See BOOKS for the full design.
*/

Pull a book on blueprints.
    Bind series of step to blueprint:

        /* ⚠ A binary's name is the platform's business. `OS` is the one variable Windows sets and
           POSIX does not, so the absence is the answer elsewhere — and a blueprint is an ordinary
           program, so it can simply ask. */
        Define suffix as ".exe" when (the environment variable "OS" but void is "") is "Windows_NT", otherwise "".

        Return a series of step with (
            a record with (
                the name "shell",
                the needs a series of text with ("tools/shell.cufe", "tools/terminal.cufe"),
                the makes a series of text with ("tools/shell{suffix}"),
                the runs a series of text with ("cufet", "build","tools/shell.cufe")),
            a record with (
                the name "repl",
                the needs a series of text with ("tools/repl.cufe", "tools/terminal.cufe"),
                the makes a series of text with ("tools/repl{suffix}"),
                the runs a series of text with ("cufet", "build","tools/repl.cufe"))).
    Done.
Done.
